      "summaries": {
        "en": "openwork is an open-source alternative to Claude Cowork, built on top of opencode to provide a collaborative coding environment for teams. It solves the problem of vendor lock-in and limited customization in existing AI pair-programming tools. Technically, it leverages TypeScript and modular agent workflows, allowing developers to inspect, modify, and extend the underlying automation logic. You can self-host it, connect it to your favorite models, and integrate it into your CI/CD pipeline. Typical use cases include automated code review, multi-agent task delegation, and building custom AI-assisted development workflows tailored to your team's needs.",
